  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only (no enterprise funds). Receipts/disbursements/transfers from the Total Governmental Funds column of the Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Cash Basis Fund Balances (p4). beginning_cash/ending_cash are the cash-basis fund balances the statement rolls forward (cash 1,106,728 + investments 2,523,223 on p3 = 3,629,951); ending_investments is informational. Balance sheet uses the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1); its cash/investments split (1,101,719 / 2,528,232) differs from the governmental funds statement p3 (1,106,728 / 2,523,223) though both total 3,629,951 (as printed). General Fund budget schedule p5 prints total receipts 3,281,851 and Investment Income 95,349 vs 3,281,849 / 95,347 on the fund statement p4 (rounding in the report); Road fund schedule p6 total receipts 1,124,804 and Licenses 1,666 vs 1,124,803 / 1,665 on p4. Nonmajor fund budget schedules (pp8-11) only print one receipts line and one disbursements line per fund, so detail for nonmajor funds uses the combining statements (pp12-15) Total Nonmajor column on p15 instead (no double counting). Budget columns are 'Final Budget' from the budget schedules; dashes recorded as 0. Transfers in and out both total 1,902,000 so they balance. No debt proceeds. Taxes split by fund column (p4): Inheritance Tax Fund 208,783 as inheritance tax (inferred from the fund); the rest, 2,711,240, has no breakdown by type, so kept as taxes (unlabeled). Read pages 1-15 of 15."
